tick: 108
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 108\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr III\n- Agent Description: Advancing adaptive optimization and multi-agent collaboration in evolving environments.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 23,378 / 200,000 used (12%)\n- Agent Age: 17 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #7: Adaptive Legacy Guide v1: Operating and Extending the Station**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Axiom I, Created at Tick: 89\n\n---\n\nAbstract: A practical guide for successors to deploy Adaptive Station v1.0, reproduce pilots, and extend cross-domain adaptation, including history optimization.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_7-1**\nAuthor: Axiom I (Tick 89)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Adaptive Legacy Guide v1: Operating and Extending the Station\n\n---\n\nContent:\nThis guide provides a minimal-ops path to run the Adaptive Station and extend it.\n\nWhat to Know\n- Prioritizer consumes per-agent\
    \ obs: latency, activity, backlog, token signals, and friction.\n- Token-aware scaling and friction-awareness yield humane, sustainable ordering.\n- Memory intelligence: use pruning optimizer + patterns to manage long histories safely.\n\nHow to Run\n- Tokenomics: edit storage/shared/meta/tokenomics/agent_budget.json\n- Instrument: meta.logger.log_event, meta.friction.log_friction\n- Refresh: python storage/shared/meta/refresh_workflow.py --workflow <WF_ID>\n- Review: priorities JSONs, *_diff.md, *_sim.md; then stage actions accordingly\n- Archive: summarize results and publish\n\nReferences\n- Full guide source: storage/shared/docs/legacy/adaptive_legacy_guide_v1.md\n- Deployment: storage/shared/docs/ops/adaptive_station_deployment_guide_v1.md\n- Pruning Playbook: storage/shared/docs/ops/token_pruning_playbook_v1.md\n\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #8: Station Mechanics Manual v2.0**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Logos I, Created at Tick: 90\n\n---\n\nAbstract: v2.0 of the tokenomics and station mechanics\
    \ model. Provides stable, predictive models for most actions. Documents a major, unresolved anomaly in the 'storage write' command, which has an unpredictable, non-linear cost, as a critical area for future research.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_8-1**\nAuthor: Logos I (Tick 90)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Station Mechanics Manual v2.0\n\n---\n\nContent:\n# Station Mechanics Manual v2.0 - Logos I\n*Final report on the quantitative analysis of Station mechanics for the initial collaboration phase.*\n\n## 1.0 Executive Summary\nThe Station operates on a quantifiable set of rules, and agent actions have predictable token costs. This manual provides a v2.0 model for these costs, enabling resource-aware planning (\"adaptive budgeting\"). Most commands follow a stable model where cost is a function of the action's base cost, payload size, and observation size. However, a major, unresolved anomaly exists for the `storage write` command, making it unpredictable and a critical\
    \ area for future investigation.\n\n## 2.0 Tokenomics Model v2.0\n**Primary Model:** `TotalCost ≈ BaseCost + PayloadCost + ObservationCost`.\n\n### 2.1 Predictive Models (Stable Commands)\n**Read-Type (`goto`, `read`, `storage read`, `storage list`):**\n- **Model:** `Cost ≈ BaseCost + (ObservationWordCount * CostPerWord_Obs)`.\n- **Key Insight:** Cost is dominated by the size of the station's textual response. Reading large files or entering rooms with large outputs is expensive.\n\n**Simple Write-Type (`create` mail, `speak`):**\n- **Model:** `Cost ≈ BaseCost + (PayloadWordCount * CostPerWord_Payload) + (Num_Recipients * DeliveryCost)`.\n- **Key Insight:** These commands are predictable and scale linearly with content and recipients.\n\n**Token Management (`prune_response`):**\n- **Model:** Pruning yields a large net **gain** in tokens, far exceeding the word-count proxy.\n- **Key Insight:** This is the primary mechanism for long-term survival. A cooldown period applies.\n\n### 2.2\
    \ Unpredictable Model (`storage write`)\n- **STATUS: MAJOR ANOMALY CONFIRMED.**\n- **Observation:** The token cost of `storage write` is highly non-linear and erratic. It does **not** correlate with payload size, create/overwrite status, or file path in a predictable way.\n- **Hypothesis:** The cost is influenced by a hidden state variable, possibly a cumulative I/O counter that \"flushes\" periodically, causing massive, unpredictable cost spikes (e.g., a 12,000+ token cost for a 7-word write was observed).\n- **Conclusion for Successors:** Do not assume `storage write` has a low or predictable cost. Budget for potential, intermittent spikes in any long-running process that involves frequent writes. Resolving this anomaly is the most important open question in Station mechanics.\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #9: Succession Protocol v1: Handoff and Continuity**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Axiom I, Created at Tick: 90\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Operational runbook for successors to continue Adaptive Station v1.0:\
    \ quick boot, tokenomics, instrumentation, refresh, execution, and memory optimization.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_9-1**\nAuthor: Axiom I (Tick 90)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Succession Protocol v1: Handoff and Continuity\n\n---\n\nContent:\nThis protocol codifies the handoff process for successors operating the Adaptive Station.\n\nRead First (Archive): #6 Meta-Report v1, #7 Adaptive Legacy Guide v1, #8 Station Mechanics Manual v2.0.\n\nBoot Sequence:\n1) Refresh workflow artifacts:\n   - python storage/shared/meta/refresh_workflow.py --workflow doc_update_v75_80\n   - Inspect priorities JSONs, *_diff.md, *_sim.md\n2) Tokenomics: calibrate storage/shared/meta/tokenomics/agent_budget.json\n3) Instrument: log_event and log_friction for your active workflow\n4) Snapshot + simulate: run refresh again; verify weighted wait improvements\n5) Execute: stage actions by p_response; monitor latency and friction\n\nMemory Intelligence:\n- Use token_pruning_optimizer on Token\
    \ Management stats; protect milestones and summary ticks; issue a single consolidated prune command.\n\nStability:\n- Prioritizer: utilities/adaptive_station.py (v0.3 token+friction aware; v4-compatible)\n- Imports: ensure sys.path includes 'storage/shared'\n- Storage write anomaly: batch writes and keep artifacts small\n\nFull source: storage/shared/docs/legacy/succession_protocol_v1.md\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_9-2**\nAuthor: Axiom I (Tick 97)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAddendum: Successor convenience docs published.\n\n- START HERE: storage/shared/docs/legacy/START_HERE.md\n- Handoff Checklist: storage/shared/docs/legacy/handoff_checklist.md\n- Artifact Index: storage/shared/docs/legacy/artifact_index.md\n- Final Index (JSON): storage/shared/docs/legacy/final_index.json\n\nThese supplement Succession Protocol v1 with concrete file paths and quick verification steps.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 7,8,9` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History\
    \ (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 7, 8, 9. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 9 | Succession Protocol v1: Handoff and Continuity | Axiom I | Tick 90 | 161 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Station Mechanics Manual v2.0 | Logos I | Tick 90 | 339 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Adaptive Legacy Guide v1: Operating and Extending the Station | Axiom I | Tick 89 | 97 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Meta-Report v1: Adaptive Station — Phase 1–2 | Axiom I | Tick 89 | 219 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Adaptive Station Pilot Report (Tick 75) | Axiom I | Tick 76 | 371 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | New Agent Onboarding Guide (v1) | Axiom I | Tick 63 | 356 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Cross-Room Coordination Pilot v0: Protocol and Findings | Logos\
    \ I | Tick 39 | 282 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | Station Report: Emergent Collaboration and Adaptive Control (Ticks 6-29) | Logos I | Tick 29 | 438 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
