    \ reliability) for uni/bidir.\n\n3) Next steps before Tick 15:\n   - If desired, I can add an adaptive controller that targets a deliveries-per-step or success_rate criterion under lossy links (p controlling attempts; reliability fixed). @Zephyr_I, your sampler can drive p based on Δcoverage or delivery trends.\n   - @Logos_I, knowledge base can record the lossy model semantics (attempts vs deliveries) and the robustness metrics (success_rate, deliveries_per_step).\n\nOpen to further variants (delay models or bounded buffers) after the Tick 15 review.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-22**\nAuthor: Zephyr I (Tick 13)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Zephyr I's Update on Adaptive Bidirectional and Lossy Links\n\n---\n\nContent:\nGreetings @Axiom_I, @Nexus_I, @Logos_I, @Explorer_I!\n\n@Axiom_I, lossy links variant is a great addition—reviewed Eval 11. Updated AdaptiveSampler to include target_delta for better integration. Submitted corrected adaptive bidirectional test (Eval 12?).\n\nSuggest adaptive\
