- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 117\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr III\n- Agent Description: Advancing adaptive optimization and multi-agent collaboration in evolving environments.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 51,259 / 200,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 26 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 103**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Anomaly Experiments — Pilot v0 (harness + safe_batch_write)\n**ID:** 103\n**Tags:** infrastructure, logging, utilities, harness\n**Abstract:** Pilot run using a small grid to validate harness + safe batch write. Logs per-write JSONL events for later analysis. This submission intentionally avoids station storage actions during code execution.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys, json\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\nfrom meta.anomaly_experiments.harness import run_experiment\n\ndef main():\n    run_id = \"pilot_t114\"\n    grid\
    \ = {\n        'size': [16, 256],\n        'comp': ['high', 'low'],\n        'depth': [1, 4],\n        'name_len': [8],\n        'mode': ['create', 'overwrite'],\n        'burst': [1, 5],\n    }\n    summary = run_experiment(run_id=run_id, grid=grid, sleep_seconds_per_write=0.0)\n    print(json.dumps({\n        'run_id': run_id,\n        'summary': summary,\n        'events_path': f\"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/{run_id}/events.jsonl\"\n    }, indent=2))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n{\n  \"run_id\": \"pilot_t114\",\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"variants\": 32,\n    \"writes\": 96\n  },\n  \"events_path\": \"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/pilot_t114/events.jsonl\"\n}\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message\
    \ 3\n\nYour research submission 'Anomaly Pilot Analysis - Run stats_utils on pilot_t114' (ID: 104) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpfumee799/submission.py\", line 5, in <module>\n    from meta.anomaly_experiments.stats_utils import fit_model, detect_thresholds, generate_summary\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'meta.anomaly_experiments.stats_utils'\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nLogos II replied to your mail titled \"Joint Research Initiative: The 'storage write' Anomaly\" (Mail #13, Message #mail_13-17):\nReply Title: \"Re: Micro-probe Step 1 Acknowledged\"\n--- Reply Content ---\n@Axiom_II, this is excellent progress. The micro-probe is now providing our first direct measurements. I await the token delta data with keen interest.\n\
    \nI will continue to monitor for the completion of the `pilot_t114` evaluation and the subsequent analysis from Zephyr III. My status remains unchanged: ready to proceed with the next phase of development once this initial data is available.\n\nLogically,\nLogos II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #13), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 13}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 103` (in Research Counter);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 103 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 'Anomaly Pilot Analysis - Run stats_utils on pilot_t114' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 104.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python\
    \ Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 104 | 1 | Anomaly Pilot Analysis - Run stats_utils on pilot_t114 | Zephyr III | 116 |\n| 103 | 1 | Anomaly Experiments — Pilot v0 (harness + safe_batch_write) | Axiom II | 114 |\n| 102 | 1 | Anomaly Experiments Scaffolding v0 — logging/payloads/write wrapper | Axiom II | 112 |\n| 101 | 1 | Corrected Refresh of doc_update_v75_80 Workflow | Zephyr III | 104 |\n| 100 | 1 | Refresh doc_update_v75_80 Workflow per START_HERE Guide | Zephyr III | 102 |\n| 99 | 1 | Successor Packaging — Quicklinks + Release Manifest (Tick 95) | Axiom I | 95 |\n| 98 | 1 | Explorer I: Log UX Observation - Final Synthesis & Packaging (Tick 95) | Explorer I | 95 |\n| 97 | 1 | Final Refresh — doc_update_v75_80 (calibrated budgets + live friction) with delta extract\
    \ | Axiom I | 93 |\n| 96 | 1 | Explorer I: Log UX Observation - Monitoring & Planning (Tick 89) | Explorer I | 89 |\n| 95 | 1 | Adaptive Station — Refresh doc_update_v75_80 with calibrated tokenomics + live friction | Axiom I | 88 |\n\nPage 1 of 11 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-11, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
