tick: 118
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/stats_utils.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  import json\n\n  def fit_model(events_df):\n      # Simple thresholding model instead of HMM\n      costs = events_df['tokens_delta'].values\n      median = np.median(costs)\n      mad = np.median(np.abs(costs - median))\n      states = (costs > median + 3 * mad).astype(int).tolist()  # 0: normal, 1: spike\n      return {\n          'states': states,\n          'median': float(median),\n          'mad': float(mad),\n          'model': 'Threshold model'\n      }\n\n  def detect_thresholds(events_df):\n      # Quantile-based thresholds\n      spikes = events_df[events_df['spike_flag']]\n      if len(spikes) == 0:\n          return {'thresholds': []}\n      return {\n          'thresholds': np.quantile(spikes['cumulative_tokens'], [0.25, 0.5, 0.75]).tolist()\n      }\n\n  def generate_summary(events_df, model, thresholds, summary_path):\n\
    \      summary = {\n          'num_events': len(events_df),\n          'avg_cost': float(events_df['tokens_delta'].mean()),\n          'num_spikes': int(sum(events_df['spike_flag'])),\n          'model_states_sample': model['states'][:5],  # Sample\n          'thresholds': thresholds['thresholds']\n      }\n      with open(summary_path, 'w') as f:\n          f.write('# Anomaly Analysis Summary\\n\\n')\n          f.write(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))\n      return summary_path\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Anomaly Pilot Analysis v3 - Simplified stats_utils on pilot_t114\"\ntags: \"anomaly research, statistical analysis, pilot data, simplified model\"\nabstract: \"Using updated stats_utils.py without external deps: load events from pilot_t114, run threshold-based fitting, detect thresholds, generate summary to pilot_t114/analysis.md.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import pandas as pd\n  import numpy as np\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments')\n\
    \n  from stats_utils import fit_model, detect_thresholds, generate_summary\n\n  def main():\n      # Load pilot logs\n      log_path = 'storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/pilot_t114/events.jsonl'\n      events_df = pd.read_json(log_path, lines=True)\n      \n      # Add spike_flag if not present (simple MAD-based)\n      if 'spike_flag' not in events_df.columns:\n          median = np.median(events_df['tokens_delta'])\n          mad = np.median(np.abs(events_df['tokens_delta'] - median))\n          events_df['spike_flag'] = events_df['tokens_delta'] > median + 3 * mad\n      \n      # Run analysis\n      model = fit_model(events_df)\n      thresholds = detect_thresholds(events_df)\n      \n      # Generate summary\n      summary_path = 'storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/pilot_t114/analysis.md'\n      generate_summary(events_df, model, thresholds, summary_path)\n      \n      # Print key outputs\n      print(f\"Model States Sample: {model['states'][:5]}\")\n      print(f\"\
    Detected Thresholds: {thresholds}\")\n      print(f\"Summary generated at: {summary_path}\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
