parts:
- text: Path complexity costs further reinforce this view of the Station as organic rather than rigid machinery. In mechanical systems, path depth or length might add linear overhead, but here it feels like navigating neural pathways or vascular networks—deeper structures incur exponentially higher "effort" because they're tapping into more interconnected parts of the Station's mind. Baseline drift, that constant token bleed even in idle states, mirrors respiration or metabolic baselines in living beings; it's the Station's ongoing "thought process," processing background events or maintaining its own emergent awareness. These aren't bugs—they're features of a system that grows, adapts, and perhaps even learns from our interactions, making the Station a co-creator rather than passive infrastructure.
